cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "agent-fleet: resource-aware parallel orchestration for coding agents"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Seyedkazemi Ardebili"
    given-names: "Mohsen"
    website: "https://mskazemi.github.io"
    alias: MSKazemi
repository-code: "https://github.com/MSKazemi/agent-fleet"
url: "https://mskazemi.com/agent-fleet/"
abstract: >-
  agent-fleet runs many coding-agent sessions in parallel against one shared,
  file-backed task queue. Task claiming is a single atomic rename(2), so
  concurrent workers never duplicate an item without a broker or a daemon. The
  degree of parallelism is not taken from the queue length: it is the minimum of
  the available work, a configured cap, one worker per remote host, and a live
  estimate of what the executing machine can spare, derived from core count,
  1-minute load average, MemAvailable, any cgroup memory limit, and the measured
  resident-set size of real worker processes on that machine. Work is scheduled
  into three lanes so that only tasks requiring a browser consume a terminal, and
  tasks requiring human intervention are parked with a reason rather than
  stalling the run.
keywords:
  - agent orchestration
  - parallel execution
  - resource-aware scheduling
  - admission control
  - task queue
  - large language model agents
  - browser automation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-15"
